# Models that basalt-voice-fetch can download for the desktop's voice
# (speech to text, voice activity detection, text to speech). Model files
# are never part of a package or of the source tree; they are downloaded
# on request and checked against the SHA-256 below before they are used.
#
# Columns: name  sha256  size_bytes  license  url
#
# Every URL is pinned to a revision of the publisher's repository on
# Hugging Face. Licenses were read at those revisions:
#   whisper.cpp ggml conversions of OpenAI Whisper: MIT (Whisper weights
#   are MIT); Silero VAD v5.1.2 (ggml conversion by ggml-org): MIT.
#   Piper voices: only voices trained from scratch on public-domain data
#   are listed (LJ Speech, LibriVox readings by Kristin and Norman, John
#   fine-tuned from Kristin). Most other English Piper voices are
#   fine-tuned from the "lessac" voice, whose dataset license (Blizzard
#   2013) does not allow redistribution for commercial use: not listed.
# Whisper models named .en understand English only; the others
# (ggml-base, ggml-small, their q5_1 quantizations, large-v3-turbo) are
# multilingual: a person's speech language other than English needs one.
# No Piper voice for another language is listed: at the pinned revision
# every Portuguese voice (pt_BR cadu, faber, jeff; pt_PT tugão) is
# fine-tuned from "lessac", or from "ryan" (CC BY-NC-SA data) with CC BY
# data of its own (pt_BR edresson). Answers in those languages are shown
# and not spoken.
# A Piper voice is two entries: the model (.onnx) and its settings (.json).
